Revision history for Perl extension Unpack-Custom

{{$NEXT}}

    - sevenzip params are no longer modified nor shared between files and
      extract calls; multivolume exclusions are per file and shell-quoted
    - the state of a run ($self->{var}) is reset for every extract call
    - Unpack::Custom::Ordinary: archive entries can't be written outside
      the destination (path traversal)
    - errors when writing files are fatal instead of silently ignored
    - extract dies when files are not an ARRAY ref, a file does not exist
      or destination is missing; a file named '0' no longer stops the queue
    - Unpack::Custom::Recursive: the same content given or found several
      times is processed once, corrupted files are deleted only when written
      for the corrupted entry, names.txt is escaped and sorted
    - new Unpack::Custom::Recursive options max_depth and max_extracted_size
    - callbacks are real methods instead of AUTOLOAD
    - the archive listing is reused and passwords are used when listing
    - removed debug output and unused dependencies, fixed cpanfile
    - documentation, tests cleanup, GitHub Actions instead of Travis
    - original version
